(391,824,'An acute diarrheal disease endemic in India and Southeast Asia whose causative agent is VIBRIO CHOLERAE. This condition can lead to severe dehydration in a matter of hours unless quickly treated.','en',2,'2026-05-29 23:29:32',NULL,NULL,'6722FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(392,826,'DEF: Includes gestational impaired glucose tolerance and gestational diabetes mellitus. DESC: Glucose tolerance changes during pregnancy; two hours after 75G glucose: venous glusose &amp;gt;= 7.8 mmol/L but &amp;lt; 11.1 mmol/L means Impaired Glucose Tolerance; venous glucose &amp;gt;= 11.1 means Diabetes Mellitus. REF: Oxford Clinical Medicine.','en',2,'2026-05-29 23:29:32',2,'2026-05-29 23:32:54','1401FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
