(1048,2209,'Motor behavior that is repetitive, often seemingly driven, and nonfunctional. This behavior markedly interferes with normal activities or results in severe bodily self-injury. The behavior is not due to the direct physiological effects of a substance or a general medical condition. (DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2026-05-29 23:34:52',NULL,NULL,'7723FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1049,2210,'A variant of bullous erythema multiforme. It ranges from mild skin and mucous membrane lesions to a severe, sometimes fatal systemic disorder. Ocular symptoms include ulcerative conjunctivitis, keratitis, iritis, uveitis, and sometimes blindness. The cause of the disease is unknown.','en',2,'2026-05-29 23:34:52',NULL,NULL,'7720FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
